<title>USA: U.S. cash soymeal - Cash offers edge lower.</title>
<headline>U.S. cash soymeal - Cash offers edge lower.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rail and truck soymeal basis offers weakened again with dealers attributing the pressure to ample supplies of soymeal and other feed ingredients.</p>
<p>Hot weather in the South and Southeast has slowed hog and poultry feed consumption, and the advancing winter wheat harvest has made low-cost wheat available for feeding.</p>
<p>One dealer said corn gluten feed and other feed items normally exported to Europe have been diverted to the domestic feed market, because Europe was buying less U.S. feed.</p>
<p>Also, recent buying of June soymeal has covered feed needs for a while.</p>
<p>They said June's price discount to July soymeal encouraged buyers to stock up this month.  </p>
